      "slug": "criar-rapido-avancado",
      "title": "Quick or detailed creation",
      "body": "**Quick:** the New task field. Type and press Enter. It covers almost everything.\n\n**Detailed:** the button next to the field, the **New** menu or `Alt+Shift+N`. It opens a panel with page, description, due date, priority, repeat, sets and labels. `Ctrl+Enter` creates.\n\n## Editing later\n\nTap the task's arrow (or `Enter` with it selected) to open the **panel**: description (up to 10,000 characters; when empty, \"+ Add description\" shows), date, priority, weight, time, subtasks, assignees, dependencies, page fields and comments. Each field saves when you leave it.\n\nAt the top of the panel, **Simple ▾** shows only the essentials; switch to **Full** to see time, sets, weight, dependencies, fields, approval, My day and history. Whatever the task already uses shows even in Simple.\n\n## The New menu\n\n`Alt+N` (or the **New** button) and a letter: **T** task, **P** page, **F** folder, **J** project, **H** habit. The task goes to the open page (or to a page of the open folder); anywhere else, to the Inbox.\n\n## Attachments\n\nIn the panel, **Attach** adds a photo (from the gallery or, on the phone, the camera) or a file to the task. Photos are shrunk on the device before uploading (to fit a 2048 px square), so they take little space; the list shows only the thumbnail and the full photo downloads when you open it. Each file can be up to **10 MB**, and each account has **1 GB** (see your usage in Settings). Whoever sees the task sees its attachments; whoever can edit it attaches and removes. Offline, the attachment waits on the device and uploads by itself later."
